      "excerpt": "Liquid plant extracts, explained. What they are, how they are used and what to keep in mind before buying one.",
      "content": "<p>Mother tinctures are liquid extracts made from plants, minerals or other natural substances. They are the starting point from which homoeopathic potencies are prepared.<\/p><h2>How are they taken?<\/h2><p>Typically, a few drops are diluted in water and taken two or three times a day. Because they are less diluted than tablets, they can have a stronger taste and a more direct action.<\/p><h2>Things to remember<\/h2><ul><li>Shake the bottle well before every use.<\/li><li>Use the measuring dropper provided — more is not always better.<\/li><li>Store in a cool, dark place, tightly closed.<\/li><li>Consult a practitioner for long-term use, pregnancy or for children.<\/li><\/ul><p>Our Mother Tinctures range is prepared with care and sealed with clear labelling, so you always know exactly what you are using.<\/p>"
